{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-8\nattempt=1\nbase=8176819d1e41f9153dbcce608c0965192b6ac5a3\ncandidate=071ff20f9a9e760d635d24bdd7873160a3471345\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\n\n### Why\n\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents th\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=071ff20f9a9e760d635d24bdd7873160a3471345 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=071ff20f9a9e760d635d24bdd7873160a3471345 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"094e85c9-70ec-46cd-95c2-504342bfcb89"}
