","stdout":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n  \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |\\n| Hard-delete rows | Breaks pin FK / audit; product soft-delete + 409 on edit |\\n| Tombstone deleted messages in channel history | Product allows either; **excluding** from listings is simpler for SPA empty states and matches “disappear”; pins still resolve via store for already-pinned ids |\\n| Nested threads (reply-to-reply) | Product is parent/replies one level; reject deep `parent_id` with 400 |\\n| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |\\n| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |\\n| Create full `files` upload schema here | Owned by MARATHON-10; accept `file_ids` but 400 when unsatisfiable |\\n| Allow any workspace member to post in public without join | Diverges from pin write rule (must be channel member) |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\n`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: nested `author` is full `UserObj` via `row_to_user_obj` / joined columns.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: workspace slug/`owner_id`; roles; non-member → **404** (no leak); privilege lack → **403**.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"username\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": null, \\\"avatar_url\\\": null, \\\"status_text\\\": null, \\\"status_emoji\\\": null },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-23T00:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `reply_count` | Count of **non-deleted** children with `parent_id = this.id` |\\n| `edited_at` | `null` until first successful PATCH; then UTC Z timestamp |\\n| `files` | `FileObj[]` (see MARATHON-10). Until files exist / attach works → always `[]` |\\n| `reactions` | `ReactionObj[]` aggregated (below) |\\n| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |\\n\\n#### `ReactionObj`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"user_ids\\\": [\\\"uuid-a\\\", \\\"uuid-b\\\"] }\\n```\\n\\nProduct name for the emoji field is **`emoji`** (not `name`). Do not add a `me` boolean; clients derive that from `user_ids` containing the caller id.\\n\\n- Group by exact `emoji` string.\\n- `count` = `len(user_ids)`.\\n- `user_ids` ordered by reaction `created_at ASC`, then `user_id ASC`.\\n- Reaction groups ordered by first-reaction `created_at ASC`, tie-break `emoji ASC`.\\n\\n#### `FileObj` (embed only; created by MARATHON-10)\\n\\n`{id, uploader_id, filename, content_type, size, created_at}` per product Files section — M8 returns `files: []` unless MARATHON-10 rows are resolvable.\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Empty/whitespace body; body too long; bad `limit`/`before`; bad `parent_id`; bad `emoji`; non-empty unsatisfiable `file_ids`; `blocks` not a list when present |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Not channel member on write; not author on PATCH; not author/owner on DELETE; private read without membership |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | PATCH or react on soft-deleted message |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write on archived channel |\\n\\n### Authz helpers (implement once, reuse)\\n\\nMirror MARATHON-7 pin access:\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_read(channel, user)`** — same rules as `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_write(channel, user)`** — channel **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).\\n\\nFor message-id routes: load message → load channel → apply read or write helper; missing message → **404** (do not leak across workspaces).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |\\n| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello @alice\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"file_ids\\\": [],\\n  \\\"blocks\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n\\n- `body` required string; after Unicode trim of leading/trailing whitespace, length **1..4000** code points; empty/whitespace-only → **400**.\\n- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.\\n- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.\\n- `blocks` optional; if present must be a **JSON array** (elements unchecked beyond JSON); persist as `blocks_json`; **not** included in `MessageObj` response keys.\\n- Unknown fields ignored.\\n\\n**Response:** `201 { \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`\\n\\n**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=\\u0026before=`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; initial load + scroll-up with `before=\\u003coldest_seen_id\\u003e`; keep prior list on error; render newest at bottom per UI |\\n| **Server** | Authz read; return **only top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`) **non-deleted** messages; **newest-first** |\\n\\n**Query:**\\n\\n- `limit` optional int, default **50**, min 1, max **100**; invalid → 400.\\n- `before` optional message id cursor: return messages strictly older than the cursor message’s (`created_at`, `id`) pair within the same channel; cursor must be a message in this channel (deleted cursor still OK as position); unknown id → **400**.\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"messages\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`\\n\\nEach element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |\\n| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown → 404 (after read visibility check on channel).\\n- `caller.id != author_id` → **403**.\\n- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.\\n- Archived channel → **423**.\\n- Same body validation as create (empty → 400).\\n- `parent_id` / `file_ids` **not** patchable in this task (ignore if sent).\\n- **200** `{ \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`; call `publish_message_updated` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Remove row from UI on 200; treat repeat delete as success |\\n| **Server** | Soft-delete; idempotent |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404 (visibility as read).\\n- Allowed if `caller.id == author_id` **OR** `caller.id == workspace.owner_id`; else **403**.\\n- Archived → **423** (mutating).\\n- If already `deleted_at` set → still **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}` (no-op).\\n- Else set `deleted_at=now`; clear reaction rows for that message (so they “no longer count”); leave pin row if any (pin list uses tombstone mapping — see edge cases).\\n- **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}`; call `publish_message_deleted` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (thread panel)** | Bearer; render oldest-first; bump parent reply badge from parent `reply_count` |\\n| **Server** | Authz read via parent’s channel; return non-deleted children **oldest-first** |\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"replies\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`  \\n(Product name is **`replies`**, not `messages`.)\\n\\n- Unknown parent → 404.\\n- Parent deleted → still allow listing non-deleted replies (or 404 — **choose: 404** if parent missing/deleted to match “disappear”).\\n- No `limit` required in this task (return all replies); if \\u003e1000, still return all for v1 (document; optional soft cap out of scope).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ reactions\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions` body `{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\" }` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [ReactionObj, ...] }`\\n\\n- Authz: channel **write** membership + writable (423 if archived).\\n- Message missing → 404; deleted → **409**.\\n- `emoji` required non-empty string; max **32** code points; reject whitespace-only; allow Unicode emoji and shortcodes as opaque strings (no server-side emoji validation library).\\n- Insert ignore if `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` exists (idempotent).\\n- Return **full** aggregated `reactions` for that message (not only the one emoji).\\n- `publish_reaction_changed` after commit.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [...] }`\\n\\n- Same authz/404/409/423 as POST.\\n- URL-decode `emoji` path segment.\\n- Delete caller’s row if present; if absent → still 200 with current aggregate (idempotent).\\n- Return full aggregate after delete.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable send/edit/delete/react; keep prior transcript |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 400 | Inline validation (empty body, etc.) |\\n| 403 | Show forbidden; do not optimistic-post |\\n| 409 | Treat message as deleted; remove editor |\\n| 423 | Lock composer; show archived |\\n| 404 | Channel/message inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume message persisted |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Existing (v3 — unchanged DDL)\\n\\n`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.\\n\\n### Migration v4 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### Alter `messages` (optional column)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `blocks_json` | TEXT | NULL | JSON array text; omit from `MessageObj` |\\n\\nIf implementer prefers zero ALTER, store blocks in a side table — **prefer single nullable column** for simplicity.\\n\\n#### Indexes on `messages`\\n\\n- `idx_messages_channel_created` on `(channel_id, created_at DESC, id DESC)` for history.\\n- `idx_messages_parent_created` on `(parent_id, created_at ASC, id ASC)` for replies.\\n\\n#### `message_reactions`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` | | Enforces idempotent POST |\\n\\nIndex: `(message_id, created_at ASC)` for aggregate ordering.\\n\\n#### `message_files` (forward seam for MARATHON-10)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `file_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | No FK until M10 `files` exists **or** FK added in M10 |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, file_id)` | | |\\n| UNIQUE | `(file_id)` | | A file attaches to at most one message |\\n\\n**M8 behavior:** if `files` table absent, refuse non-empty `file_ids` with 400 and leave `message_files` unused. M10 creates `files` and wires validation (uploader_id == caller, not already attached).\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v4 new tables + indexes + optional column | **Yes** — additive |\\n| v3 messages columns | **Unchanged** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. Soft-deleted messages have `deleted_at` non-null; excluded from history/reply lists.\\n2. `reply_count` never includes deleted children.\\n3. At most one reaction row per `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`.\\n4. `parent_id` either NULL or points to top-level message in same channel.\\n5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.\\n6. REST `MessageObj` never carries `seq`.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` | Contract tests: post/list/pagination/edit/delete/replies/reactions/authz/423/409/empty body/parent rules/idempotent delete \\u0026 reactions; cluster read-after-write on second node |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Add PATCH, DELETE, GET replies, POST/DELETE reactions; keep pin routes; factor `_require_pin_access` into shared `_require_message_channel_access(read|write)` used by pins + CRUD + reactions |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST`/`GET /{channel_id}/messages` using messages store + same authz patterns as pins |\\n| `server/events.py` | No-op `publish_message_created/updated/deleted`, `publish_reaction_changed` with docstring payloads for M13 (`type`, `channel_id`, message/reactions fields — **seq assigned by M13**) |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring: CRUD owned here |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Only if enrichment changes assertions (prefer keep using `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`; update empty `reactions` expectations only if pins now return aggregates — still `[]` without reaction rows) |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Optionally assert v4 migration present; do not break v3 assertions |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| File upload routes | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Search / slash / read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS / Redis fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| DM create | MARATHON-9 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v4 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. `messages/store.py` enrichment + CRUD + reactions + mentions.\\n3. Channel message POST/GET routes.\\n4. Message PATCH/DELETE/replies/reactions routes.\\n5. Event no-op hooks + call sites.\\n6. `tests/test_messages.py` (+ keep pins green).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Reaction endpoints can land in parallel with list pagination once insert/get exist.\\n- Channel GET/POST messages can land before PATCH/DELETE.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `MessageObj` + POST/GET channel messages + PATCH/DELETE | MARATHON-17 SPA; MARATHON-11 search/slash (reads body); MARATHON-13 event payloads |\\n| `{replies}` oldest-first | MARATHON-17 thread panel |\\n| `{reactions}` aggregate + POST/DELETE idempotent | MARATHON-17 emoji picker |\\n| Soft-delete + 409 on edit deleted | SPA + graders |\\n| `mentions: user_id[]` from `@username` | MARATHON-11 extends forms / mention_count |\\n| `file_ids` accept + `message_files` / 400 seam | MARATHON-10 attach rules |\\n| No-op message/reaction publish hooks | MARATHON-13 assigns dense `seq` + WS frames |\\n| Pin embed still `MessageObj` | Existing pin UI / tests |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-7 closed: v3 messages, pins, `assert_channel_writable`, channel membership matrix.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- File upload + ownership attach enforcement details → MARATHON-10 (may tighten `file_ids` validation once `files` exists).\\n- Slash commands + `@channel`/`@here`/`@group` + read_state → MARATHON-11.\\n- Dense seq + WS resume → MARATHON-13.\\n- SPA transcript UI → MARATHON-17.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/files` multipart + download | future `server/files/*` | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Slash `/me` `/shrug` `/topic` … interception | message POST body | MARATHON-11 (M8 stores literal body) |\\n| `@channel` / `@here` / `@group-handle` | mentions | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET /api/search` | search | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS subscribe/resume + `seq` on frames | `server/events.py` real fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | DM channels | MARATHON-9 |\\n| SPA message/thread/reaction UI | `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Changing pin route semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` pin | Already shipped; only share helpers/enrichment |\\n| IRC message bridge | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/messages/store.py` — thin `MessageObj` / get | **In scope** — enrich + CRUD |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` — pin only | **In scope** — add CRUD/reactions; keep pins |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` — join/leave/pins | **In scope** — add messages POST/GET |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — `assert_channel_writable`, membership | **In scope** — reuse; no ChannelObj key changes |\\n| `server/db.py` — v3 messages | **In scope** — add v4; do not recreate messages |\\n| `server/events.py` — `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — add message/reaction no-ops |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers already mounted | **Out of scope** unless new router (none) |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` — SQL-seed messages + MSG_KEYS | **Keep green**; enrichment must preserve keys |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` — v3 schema asserts | **Keep green**; additive v4 OK |\\n| `static/js/*` — no message API yet | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| Grep: no channel messages routes yet | Greenfield under channels router |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\\n| Empty / whitespace `body` on POST/PATCH | **400** |\\n| `body` length 4000 OK; 4001 → **400** |\\n| POST without channel membership (public, workspace member only) | **403** |\\n| POST as channel member on archived | **423** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` pointing at a reply | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` in another channel | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` deleted | **400** |\\n| GET history includes replies | **Must not** — top-level only |\\n| GET history includes deleted | **Must not** |\\n| `before` on first page omitted | Newest `limit` messages |\\n| `limit=0` or `limit=101` | **400** |\\n| PATCH by non-author member | **403** |\\n| PATCH by workspace owner who is not author | **403** (owner is not enough for edit) |\\n| PATCH deleted | **409** |\\n| DELETE by author | **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE by workspace `owner_id` (not author) | **200** |\\n| DELETE by admin who is not owner_id | **403** |\\n| DELETE twice | Both **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE then GET history | Message absent |\\n| DELETE then PATCH | **409** |\\n| DELETE then POST reaction | **409** |\\n| POST reaction twice same emoji | **200**; single row; aggregate count unchanged |\\n| DELETE reaction never added | **200**; aggregate unchanged |\\n| Reaction emoji `\\\":+1:\\\"` vs `\\\"👍\\\"` | Distinct opaque strings |\\n| Mentions `@alice` mid-word `foo@alice` | No match |\\n| Mention self `@me` | Not included in `mentions` |\\n| Mention unknown user | Skipped (not 400) |\\n| `file_ids: [\\\"…\\\"]` before M10 files | **400** |\\n| `blocks: {}` (object not array) | **400** |\\n| `blocks: []` | Persist; MessageObj unchanged keys |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n| Pin list after message soft-delete | Return pin entry with tombstone `MessageObj`: `body=\\\"\\\"`, `files=[]`, `reactions=[]`, `mentions=[]`, `reply_count` as computed; **or** skip pin — **prefer tombstone** so pin list length stable |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; fail closed after timeout (no 500 envelope inventiveness) |\\n| Concurrent reaction inserts | PK conflict → treat as idempotent success |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\\\"hi\\\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.\\n2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.\\n3. `GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` → **200** `{messages}` newest-first; only top-level non-deleted; supports `limit` + `before` cursor.\\n4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.\\n5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.\\n6. `DELETE /api/messages/{id}` as author or workspace owner → **200** `{deleted:true}` idempotent; message omitted from later GET history; non-author non-owner → **403**.\\n7. `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions:[{emoji,count,user_ids}]}` idempotent per `(user,emoji)`; `DELETE .../reactions/{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions}` idempotent.\\n8. Archived channel → POST/PATCH/DELETE message and reaction mutate → **423** `archived`; GET history/replies still **200** if authorized.\\n9. Private channel non-member → read/write **403** (workspace member) or **404** (stranger), consistent with pins.\\n10. **Cluster:** POST message on `:8000`, GET on `:8001` with same token sees it (shared SQLite).\\n11. Existing pin tests remain green; pin embed still exposes full `MessageObj` keys.\\n12. **Negative:** must **not** put `seq` on `MessageObj`; must **not** interpret slash commands; must **not** drop/recreate `messages` table; must **not** allow reply-to-reply; must **not** return deleted messages in channel history; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_messages.py`)\\n\\n- Happy path create → list ordering → pagination with `before`.\\n- Thread create + replies ordering + `reply_count`.\\n- Edit sets `edited_at`; edit deleted → 409; delete idempotent; owner delete.\\n- Reactions aggregate shape, idempotent POST/DELETE, multi-user counts.\\n- Authz matrix: non-member, private, archived 423, author-only patch.\\n- Mentions: `@user` resolved; mid-word ignored; self excluded.\\n- `file_ids` non-empty → 400 (until files seeded/M10).\\n- Migration v4 applied; reverse drops v4 objects without destroying v3 unexpectedly in reverse tests (follow existing reverse pattern).\\n- Regression: run `tests/test_pins.py` + `tests/test_channels.py`.\\n\\n### Manual / human\\n\\n1. Boot cluster via `start.sh` (do not required for architect; implementer verifies).\\n2. Register two users; create workspace; join `#general`.\\n3. POST messages; confirm GET newest-first; reply; open replies oldest-first.\\n4. React twice; confirm count 1; second user react; count 2; delete own reaction.\\n5. Delete message; confirm absent from list; PATCH returns 409.\\n6. Archive channel; confirm POST message 423; unarchive; POST works.\\n7. Repeat GET against another node port to confirm shared DB.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"IMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.573541406Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:58:38.587406482Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Note: depends on channels task. POST channels/{id}/messages {body,parent_id?,file_ids?,blocks?}; empty body 400; MessageObj with author, reply_count, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner, idempotent 200 {deleted:true}. GET messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Reactions POST/DELETE idempotent per (user,emoji) return {reactions}.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.962464474Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.97263884Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-10\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.139019113Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.207494951Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 42,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=22\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:40:54.576884693Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 45,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"author\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=071ff20f9a9e760d635d24bdd7873160a3471345\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:58:38.572783754Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nagent-ipc.sock\ndaemon-agents.json\ndaemon.lock\ndaemon.pid\ndaemon.sock\nevents\n","stderr":"","executionTime":182,"interleavedOutput":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n  \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |\\n| Hard-delete rows | Breaks pin FK / audit; product soft-delete + 409 on edit |\\n| Tombstone deleted messages in channel history | Product allows either; **excluding** from listings is simpler for SPA empty states and matches “disappear”; pins still resolve via store for already-pinned ids |\\n| Nested threads (reply-to-reply) | Product is parent/replies one level; reject deep `parent_id` with 400 |\\n| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |\\n| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |\\n| Create full `files` upload schema here | Owned by MARATHON-10; accept `file_ids` but 400 when unsatisfiable |\\n| Allow any workspace member to post in public without join | Diverges from pin write rule (must be channel member) |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\n`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: nested `author` is full `UserObj` via `row_to_user_obj` / joined columns.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: workspace slug/`owner_id`; roles; non-member → **404** (no leak); privilege lack → **403**.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"username\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": null, \\\"avatar_url\\\": null, \\\"status_text\\\": null, \\\"status_emoji\\\": null },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-23T00:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `reply_count` | Count of **non-deleted** children with `parent_id = this.id` |\\n| `edited_at` | `null` until first successful PATCH; then UTC Z timestamp |\\n| `files` | `FileObj[]` (see MARATHON-10). Until files exist / attach works → always `[]` |\\n| `reactions` | `ReactionObj[]` aggregated (below) |\\n| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |\\n\\n#### `ReactionObj`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"user_ids\\\": [\\\"uuid-a\\\", \\\"uuid-b\\\"] }\\n```\\n\\nProduct name for the emoji field is **`emoji`** (not `name`). Do not add a `me` boolean; clients derive that from `user_ids` containing the caller id.\\n\\n- Group by exact `emoji` string.\\n- `count` = `len(user_ids)`.\\n- `user_ids` ordered by reaction `created_at ASC`, then `user_id ASC`.\\n- Reaction groups ordered by first-reaction `created_at ASC`, tie-break `emoji ASC`.\\n\\n#### `FileObj` (embed only; created by MARATHON-10)\\n\\n`{id, uploader_id, filename, content_type, size, created_at}` per product Files section — M8 returns `files: []` unless MARATHON-10 rows are resolvable.\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Empty/whitespace body; body too long; bad `limit`/`before`; bad `parent_id`; bad `emoji`; non-empty unsatisfiable `file_ids`; `blocks` not a list when present |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Not channel member on write; not author on PATCH; not author/owner on DELETE; private read without membership |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | PATCH or react on soft-deleted message |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write on archived channel |\\n\\n### Authz helpers (implement once, reuse)\\n\\nMirror MARATHON-7 pin access:\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_read(channel, user)`** — same rules as `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_write(channel, user)`** — channel **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).\\n\\nFor message-id routes: load message → load channel → apply read or write helper; missing message → **404** (do not leak across workspaces).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |\\n| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello @alice\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"file_ids\\\": [],\\n  \\\"blocks\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n\\n- `body` required string; after Unicode trim of leading/trailing whitespace, length **1..4000** code points; empty/whitespace-only → **400**.\\n- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.\\n- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.\\n- `blocks` optional; if present must be a **JSON array** (elements unchecked beyond JSON); persist as `blocks_json`; **not** included in `MessageObj` response keys.\\n- Unknown fields ignored.\\n\\n**Response:** `201 { \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`\\n\\n**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=\\u0026before=`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; initial load + scroll-up with `before=\\u003coldest_seen_id\\u003e`; keep prior list on error; render newest at bottom per UI |\\n| **Server** | Authz read; return **only top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`) **non-deleted** messages; **newest-first** |\\n\\n**Query:**\\n\\n- `limit` optional int, default **50**, min 1, max **100**; invalid → 400.\\n- `before` optional message id cursor: return messages strictly older than the cursor message’s (`created_at`, `id`) pair within the same channel; cursor must be a message in this channel (deleted cursor still OK as position); unknown id → **400**.\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"messages\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`\\n\\nEach element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |\\n| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown → 404 (after read visibility check on channel).\\n- `caller.id != author_id` → **403**.\\n- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.\\n- Archived channel → **423**.\\n- Same body validation as create (empty → 400).\\n- `parent_id` / `file_ids` **not** patchable in this task (ignore if sent).\\n- **200** `{ \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`; call `publish_message_updated` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Remove row from UI on 200; treat repeat delete as success |\\n| **Server** | Soft-delete; idempotent |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404 (visibility as read).\\n- Allowed if `caller.id == author_id` **OR** `caller.id == workspace.owner_id`; else **403**.\\n- Archived → **423** (mutating).\\n- If already `deleted_at` set → still **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}` (no-op).\\n- Else set `deleted_at=now`; clear reaction rows for that message (so they “no longer count”); leave pin row if any (pin list uses tombstone mapping — see edge cases).\\n- **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}`; call `publish_message_deleted` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (thread panel)** | Bearer; render oldest-first; bump parent reply badge from parent `reply_count` |\\n| **Server** | Authz read via parent’s channel; return non-deleted children **oldest-first** |\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"replies\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`  \\n(Product name is **`replies`**, not `messages`.)\\n\\n- Unknown parent → 404.\\n- Parent deleted → still allow listing non-deleted replies (or 404 — **choose: 404** if parent missing/deleted to match “disappear”).\\n- No `limit` required in this task (return all replies); if \\u003e1000, still return all for v1 (document; optional soft cap out of scope).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ reactions\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions` body `{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\" }` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [ReactionObj, ...] }`\\n\\n- Authz: channel **write** membership + writable (423 if archived).\\n- Message missing → 404; deleted → **409**.\\n- `emoji` required non-empty string; max **32** code points; reject whitespace-only; allow Unicode emoji and shortcodes as opaque strings (no server-side emoji validation library).\\n- Insert ignore if `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` exists (idempotent).\\n- Return **full** aggregated `reactions` for that message (not only the one emoji).\\n- `publish_reaction_changed` after commit.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [...] }`\\n\\n- Same authz/404/409/423 as POST.\\n- URL-decode `emoji` path segment.\\n- Delete caller’s row if present; if absent → still 200 with current aggregate (idempotent).\\n- Return full aggregate after delete.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable send/edit/delete/react; keep prior transcript |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 400 | Inline validation (empty body, etc.) |\\n| 403 | Show forbidden; do not optimistic-post |\\n| 409 | Treat message as deleted; remove editor |\\n| 423 | Lock composer; show archived |\\n| 404 | Channel/message inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume message persisted |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Existing (v3 — unchanged DDL)\\n\\n`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.\\n\\n### Migration v4 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### Alter `messages` (optional column)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `blocks_json` | TEXT | NULL | JSON array text; omit from `MessageObj` |\\n\\nIf implementer prefers zero ALTER, store blocks in a side table — **prefer single nullable column** for simplicity.\\n\\n#### Indexes on `messages`\\n\\n- `idx_messages_channel_created` on `(channel_id, created_at DESC, id DESC)` for history.\\n- `idx_messages_parent_created` on `(parent_id, created_at ASC, id ASC)` for replies.\\n\\n#### `message_reactions`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` | | Enforces idempotent POST |\\n\\nIndex: `(message_id, created_at ASC)` for aggregate ordering.\\n\\n#### `message_files` (forward seam for MARATHON-10)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `file_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | No FK until M10 `files` exists **or** FK added in M10 |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, file_id)` | | |\\n| UNIQUE | `(file_id)` | | A file attaches to at most one message |\\n\\n**M8 behavior:** if `files` table absent, refuse non-empty `file_ids` with 400 and leave `message_files` unused. M10 creates `files` and wires validation (uploader_id == caller, not already attached).\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v4 new tables + indexes + optional column | **Yes** — additive |\\n| v3 messages columns | **Unchanged** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. Soft-deleted messages have `deleted_at` non-null; excluded from history/reply lists.\\n2. `reply_count` never includes deleted children.\\n3. At most one reaction row per `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`.\\n4. `parent_id` either NULL or points to top-level message in same channel.\\n5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.\\n6. REST `MessageObj` never carries `seq`.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` | Contract tests: post/list/pagination/edit/delete/replies/reactions/authz/423/409/empty body/parent rules/idempotent delete \\u0026 reactions; cluster read-after-write on second node |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Add PATCH, DELETE, GET replies, POST/DELETE reactions; keep pin routes; factor `_require_pin_access` into shared `_require_message_channel_access(read|write)` used by pins + CRUD + reactions |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST`/`GET /{channel_id}/messages` using messages store + same authz patterns as pins |\\n| `server/events.py` | No-op `publish_message_created/updated/deleted`, `publish_reaction_changed` with docstring payloads for M13 (`type`, `channel_id`, message/reactions fields — **seq assigned by M13**) |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring: CRUD owned here |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Only if enrichment changes assertions (prefer keep using `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`; update empty `reactions` expectations only if pins now return aggregates — still `[]` without reaction rows) |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Optionally assert v4 migration present; do not break v3 assertions |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| File upload routes | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Search / slash / read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS / Redis fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| DM create | MARATHON-9 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v4 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. `messages/store.py` enrichment + CRUD + reactions + mentions.\\n3. Channel message POST/GET routes.\\n4. Message PATCH/DELETE/replies/reactions routes.\\n5. Event no-op hooks + call sites.\\n6. `tests/test_messages.py` (+ keep pins green).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Reaction endpoints can land in parallel with list pagination once insert/get exist.\\n- Channel GET/POST messages can land before PATCH/DELETE.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `MessageObj` + POST/GET channel messages + PATCH/DELETE | MARATHON-17 SPA; MARATHON-11 search/slash (reads body); MARATHON-13 event payloads |\\n| `{replies}` oldest-first | MARATHON-17 thread panel |\\n| `{reactions}` aggregate + POST/DELETE idempotent | MARATHON-17 emoji picker |\\n| Soft-delete + 409 on edit deleted | SPA + graders |\\n| `mentions: user_id[]` from `@username` | MARATHON-11 extends forms / mention_count |\\n| `file_ids` accept + `message_files` / 400 seam | MARATHON-10 attach rules |\\n| No-op message/reaction publish hooks | MARATHON-13 assigns dense `seq` + WS frames |\\n| Pin embed still `MessageObj` | Existing pin UI / tests |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-7 closed: v3 messages, pins, `assert_channel_writable`, channel membership matrix.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- File upload + ownership attach enforcement details → MARATHON-10 (may tighten `file_ids` validation once `files` exists).\\n- Slash commands + `@channel`/`@here`/`@group` + read_state → MARATHON-11.\\n- Dense seq + WS resume → MARATHON-13.\\n- SPA transcript UI → MARATHON-17.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/files` multipart + download | future `server/files/*` | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Slash `/me` `/shrug` `/topic` … interception | message POST body | MARATHON-11 (M8 stores literal body) |\\n| `@channel` / `@here` / `@group-handle` | mentions | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET /api/search` | search | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS subscribe/resume + `seq` on frames | `server/events.py` real fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | DM channels | MARATHON-9 |\\n| SPA message/thread/reaction UI | `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Changing pin route semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` pin | Already shipped; only share helpers/enrichment |\\n| IRC message bridge | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/messages/store.py` — thin `MessageObj` / get | **In scope** — enrich + CRUD |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` — pin only | **In scope** — add CRUD/reactions; keep pins |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` — join/leave/pins | **In scope** — add messages POST/GET |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — `assert_channel_writable`, membership | **In scope** — reuse; no ChannelObj key changes |\\n| `server/db.py` — v3 messages | **In scope** — add v4; do not recreate messages |\\n| `server/events.py` — `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — add message/reaction no-ops |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers already mounted | **Out of scope** unless new router (none) |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` — SQL-seed messages + MSG_KEYS | **Keep green**; enrichment must preserve keys |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` — v3 schema asserts | **Keep green**; additive v4 OK |\\n| `static/js/*` — no message API yet | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| Grep: no channel messages routes yet | Greenfield under channels router |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\\n| Empty / whitespace `body` on POST/PATCH | **400** |\\n| `body` length 4000 OK; 4001 → **400** |\\n| POST without channel membership (public, workspace member only) | **403** |\\n| POST as channel member on archived | **423** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` pointing at a reply | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` in another channel | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` deleted | **400** |\\n| GET history includes replies | **Must not** — top-level only |\\n| GET history includes deleted | **Must not** |\\n| `before` on first page omitted | Newest `limit` messages |\\n| `limit=0` or `limit=101` | **400** |\\n| PATCH by non-author member | **403** |\\n| PATCH by workspace owner who is not author | **403** (owner is not enough for edit) |\\n| PATCH deleted | **409** |\\n| DELETE by author | **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE by workspace `owner_id` (not author) | **200** |\\n| DELETE by admin who is not owner_id | **403** |\\n| DELETE twice | Both **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE then GET history | Message absent |\\n| DELETE then PATCH | **409** |\\n| DELETE then POST reaction | **409** |\\n| POST reaction twice same emoji | **200**; single row; aggregate count unchanged |\\n| DELETE reaction never added | **200**; aggregate unchanged |\\n| Reaction emoji `\\\":+1:\\\"` vs `\\\"👍\\\"` | Distinct opaque strings |\\n| Mentions `@alice` mid-word `foo@alice` | No match |\\n| Mention self `@me` | Not included in `mentions` |\\n| Mention unknown user | Skipped (not 400) |\\n| `file_ids: [\\\"…\\\"]` before M10 files | **400** |\\n| `blocks: {}` (object not array) | **400** |\\n| `blocks: []` | Persist; MessageObj unchanged keys |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n| Pin list after message soft-delete | Return pin entry with tombstone `MessageObj`: `body=\\\"\\\"`, `files=[]`, `reactions=[]`, `mentions=[]`, `reply_count` as computed; **or** skip pin — **prefer tombstone** so pin list length stable |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; fail closed after timeout (no 500 envelope inventiveness) |\\n| Concurrent reaction inserts | PK conflict → treat as idempotent success |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\\\"hi\\\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.\\n2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.\\n3. `GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` → **200** `{messages}` newest-first; only top-level non-deleted; supports `limit` + `before` cursor.\\n4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.\\n5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.\\n6. `DELETE /api/messages/{id}` as author or workspace owner → **200** `{deleted:true}` idempotent; message omitted from later GET history; non-author non-owner → **403**.\\n7. `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions:[{emoji,count,user_ids}]}` idempotent per `(user,emoji)`; `DELETE .../reactions/{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions}` idempotent.\\n8. Archived channel → POST/PATCH/DELETE message and reaction mutate → **423** `archived`; GET history/replies still **200** if authorized.\\n9. Private channel non-member → read/write **403** (workspace member) or **404** (stranger), consistent with pins.\\n10. **Cluster:** POST message on `:8000`, GET on `:8001` with same token sees it (shared SQLite).\\n11. Existing pin tests remain green; pin embed still exposes full `MessageObj` keys.\\n12. **Negative:** must **not** put `seq` on `MessageObj`; must **not** interpret slash commands; must **not** drop/recreate `messages` table; must **not** allow reply-to-reply; must **not** return deleted messages in channel history; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_messages.py`)\\n\\n- Happy path create → list ordering → pagination with `before`.\\n- Thread create + replies ordering + `reply_count`.\\n- Edit sets `edited_at`; edit deleted → 409; delete idempotent; owner delete.\\n- Reactions aggregate shape, idempotent POST/DELETE, multi-user counts.\\n- Authz matrix: non-member, private, archived 423, author-only patch.\\n- Mentions: `@user` resolved; mid-word ignored; self excluded.\\n- `file_ids` non-empty → 400 (until files seeded/M10).\\n- Migration v4 applied; reverse drops v4 objects without destroying v3 unexpectedly in reverse tests (follow existing reverse pattern).\\n- Regression: run `tests/test_pins.py` + `tests/test_channels.py`.\\n\\n### Manual / human\\n\\n1. Boot cluster via `start.sh` (do not required for architect; implementer verifies).\\n2. Register two users; create workspace; join `#general`.\\n3. POST messages; confirm GET newest-first; reply; open replies oldest-first.\\n4. React twice; confirm count 1; second user react; count 2; delete own reaction.\\n5. Delete message; confirm absent from list; PATCH returns 409.\\n6. Archive channel; confirm POST message 423; unarchive; POST works.\\n7. Repeat GET against another node port to confirm shared DB.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"IMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.573541406Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:58:38.587406482Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Note: depends on channels task. POST channels/{id}/messages {body,parent_id?,file_ids?,blocks?}; empty body 400; MessageObj with author, reply_count, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner, idempotent 200 {deleted:true}. GET messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Reactions POST/DELETE idempotent per (user,emoji) return {reactions}.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.962464474Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.97263884Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-10\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.139019113Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.207494951Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\