ion_changed` after commit.\n\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \"reactions\": [...] }`\n\n- Same authz/404/409/423 as POST.\n- URL-decode `emoji` path segment.\n- Delete caller’s row if present; if absent → still 200 with current aggregate (idempotent).\n- Return full aggregate after delete.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable send/edit/delete/react; keep prior\n---\n==== ### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/messages at -1\n==== ## Data Model at 15010\n## Data Model\n\n### Existing (v3 — unchanged DDL)\n\n`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.\n\n### Migration v4 (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### Alter `messages` (optional column)\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `blocks_json` | TEXT | NULL | JSON array text; omit from `MessageObj` |\n\nIf implementer prefers zero ALTER, store blocks in a side table — **prefer single nullable column** for simplicity.\n\n#### Indexes on `messages`\n\n- `idx_messages_channel_created` on `(channel_id, created_at DESC, id DESC)` for history.\n- `idx_messages_parent_created` on `(parent_id, created_at ASC, id ASC)` for replies.\n\n#### `message_reactions`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\n| `emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` | | Enforces idempotent POST |\n\nIndex: `(message_id, created_at ASC)` for aggregate ordering.\n\n#### `message_files` (forward seam for MARATHON-10)\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `file_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | No FK until M10 `files` exists **or** FK added in M10 |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, file_id)` | | |\n| UNIQUE | `(file_id)` | | A file attaches to at most one message |\n\n**M8 behavior:** if `files` table absent, refuse non-empty `file_ids` with 400 and leave `message_files` unused. M10 creates `files` and wires validation (uploader_id == caller, not already attach\n---\n==== ## Acceptance at 25115\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\"hi\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.\n2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.\n3. `GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` → **200** `{messages}` newest-first; only top-level non-deleted; supports `limit` + `before` cursor.\n4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.\n5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.\n6. `DELETE /api/messages/{id}` as author or workspace owner → **200** `{deleted:true}` idempotent; message omitted from later GET history; non-author non-owner → **403**.\n7. `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions:[{emoji,count,user_ids}]}` idempotent per `(user,emoji)`; `DELETE .../reactions/{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions}` idempotent.\n8. Archived channel → POST/PATCH/DELETE message and reaction mutate → **423** `archived`; GET history/replies still **200** if authorized.\n9. Private channel non-member → read/write **403** (workspace member) or **404** (stranger), consistent with pins.\n10. **Cluster:** POST message on `:8000`, GET on `:8001` with same token sees it (shared SQLite).\n11. Existing pin tests remain green; pin embed still exposes full `MessageObj` keys.\n12. **Negative:** must **not** put `seq` on `MessageObj`; must **not** interpret slash commands; must **not** drop/recreate `messages` table; must **not** allow reply-to-reply; must **not** return deleted messages in channel history; mu\n---\n","localExecutionTimeMs":109},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract DELETE/PATCH contracts from design"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-d0c084a0-3878-4b2e-8528-6577a497a77c-22\nfc_716d688a-6191-9d86-b0c6-b3104bb70217_0","startedAtMs":"1787446812891","completedAtMs":"1787446813049"},"model_call_id":"8851f187-b2fd-43ba-8b2c-35c46d51c64d-9-ytvm","session_id":"094e85c9-70ec-46cd-95c2-504342bfcb89","timestamp_ms":1787446813072}
